        rules: {
          objective: "Get rid of all your cards. The last player remaining with cards is the 'Donkey'.",
          gameplay: '1. Starting: The player holding the Ace of Spades leads the first trick.\n2. Following Suit: Every player must follow the suit led.\n3. Winning a Trick: The highest card of the suit led wins the trick. The winner leads the next trick.\n4. The Penalty: If a player cannot follow suit, the trick ends immediately. That player must pick up all cards currently on the table and add them to their hand. That player then leads the next trick.',
          keyRules: [
            'Cards rank: A (high), K, Q, J, 10... 2 (low).',
            "A player is 'Safe' once they have no cards left.",
            'If you lead a card and everyone follows suit, the cards in the trick are discarded and removed from the game.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Get rid of your high cards (A, K, Q) as early as possible in suits where you have many cards.',
          intermediate: "If you are forced to lead a trick, lead a suit where you have only one or two cards (a 'short' suit) to increase your chance of being unable to follow suit later (which lets you dump other high cards).",
          advanced: 'Trap Tactics: If you know an opponent has no cards left in a particular suit, lead that suit to force them to take a penalty if they are the one supposed to follow suit.',
          tips: [
            "Keep your Spades safeâ€”since the game starts with the Ace of Spades, it's often the most contested suit.",
            'If you have the Ace and King of a suit, lead the Ace first to clear it out.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
